ow 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8b6ee04bda65b96e2475b9411e65a04d86e359f7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8b6ee04bda65b96e2475b9411e65a04d86e359f7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 2:22PM MDT until October 23 at 4:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River and other area streams\ncaused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache, Central Mineral and Western Rio\nGrande Counties...\n\n* WHEN...Until 445 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Conejos River, area streams, and other\nlow-lying and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\nNumerous roads remain closed due to flooding. Streams continue to\nrise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 216 PM MDT, Emergency management reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Stream gauge reports indicate that the Conejos River will be\naround it's maximum level at Mogote.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCumbres Pass, Platoro, Mogote.\n- Highway 17 between Antonito and Cumbres Pass remains closed due\nto reported water and debris over the roadway.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T16:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ca942b190f256136f565bf512509a9717e918ea5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ca942b190f256136f565bf512509a9717e918ea5.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 1:59PM MDT until October 23 at 4:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River and its tributaries is\nongoing in and around the communities of Conejos and Antonito due\nto excessive rainfall over the previous 48 hours.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 415 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Conejos River, area creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\nStreams continue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier\nrainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 157 PM MDT, Emergency management reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Stream gauges on the Conejos River and other\ntributaries, including the San Antonio River, are continuing to\nrise.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Conejos, Bountiful and Ortiz.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T16:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3117d826d0e8a763ee35a21d2fd9246bc7cdda2.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3117d826d0e8a763ee35a21d2fd9246bc7cdda2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San